[size=6][b]GK2 Mod Framework[/b][/size]

GK2 Mod Framework adds a Mods menu to Graveyard Keeper 2. It lets supported mods show their settings, compatibility status and restart requirements in the game. The framework does not change gameplay on its own.

[size=5][b]FEATURES[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Open the Mods menu from the main menu or the in-game pause menu.
[*]See registered mods, their status, dependencies and available settings.
[*]Use mouse, keyboard or controller navigation in Framework-hosted settings pages.
[*]Choose "Quit to apply" when a mod has an enable or disable change waiting for the next launch. In-game confirmation warns that unsaved progress may be lost.
[*]Framework UI translations: English, Bulgarian, German, French, Russian, Korean and Simplified Chinese.
[/list]

[size=5][b]REQUIREMENTS[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Graveyard Keeper 2 for Windows x64 on Steam. Framework 0.1.15 was tested on Steam build 25533739.
[*]BepInEx 5.4.23.5 x64, installed separately.
[/list]

[size=5][b]COMPATIBILITY[/b][/size]

Framework 0.1.15 was tested with the released GK2 Tweak Pack 0.1.2 and GK2 Ultrawide Fix 0.1.6 on Steam build 25533739. Mods that require a known game build can remain disabled after an untested game update. The Mods menu lists mods that register with the Framework; standalone BepInEx mods may still run without appearing there.

[size=5][b]INSTALLATION[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install BepInEx 5.4.23.5 x64 in the Graveyard Keeper 2 folder. Start and close the game once.
[*]Close the game, then extract the complete Framework archive into the game folder. The DLL must be at [b]BepInEx/plugins/GK2.Framework.dll[/b] and the translation files must be under [b]BepInEx/plugins/GK2.Framework/Localization[/b].
[*]Start the game and open [b]Mods[/b] from the main menu or pause menu.
[/list]

[size=5][b]UNINSTALLATION[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close the game.
[*]Remove [b]BepInEx/plugins/GK2.Framework.dll[/b] and the [b]BepInEx/plugins/GK2.Framework[/b] folder.
[/list]

Mods that require the Framework will no longer load. Existing BepInEx configuration files and save data are not removed automatically; the effect of removing a dependent mod on a save depends on that mod.

[size=5][b]KNOWN LIMITATIONS[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]The Framework does not download, update or hot-reload mods. BepInEx loads plugin DLLs.
[*]The controller on-screen keyboard currently has a Latin text layout. Use a physical keyboard to enter text in other writing systems.
[*]"Quit to apply" closes the game; relaunch it manually after any cloud synchronization has finished.
[/list]

[size=5][b]TROUBLESHOOTING[/b][/size]

[b]The Mods button is missing.[/b] Check that BepInEx loaded and that [b]BepInEx/LogOutput.log[/b] contains [b]GK2_FRAMEWORK_READY[/b].

[b]A mod is missing from the list.[/b] Only mods that register with the Framework appear. Check the mod's installation instructions and the log for its registration message.

[b]A mod shows an incompatible or unknown build.[/b] Check its details in the Mods menu. Do not force-enable a mod that reports an unsupported game build.

[size=5][b]CREDITS[/b][/size]

Framework by SuperMan4eg. The restart action was contributed through GitHub PR #4 by AcTePuKc. BepInEx is a separate requirement and is not included in this archive. The Framework license is included in the download.

